{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546000-a-theory-hypertech-and-technology-mystical-magick-and","id":1546000,"title":"A Theory: Hypertech and technology, Mystical Magick and...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-16T08:35:44-08:00","id":1546000,"title":"A Theory: Hypertech and technology, Mystical Magick and...","content":"Greetings!<br /> Been a while.<br /> <br /> This is an idea that popped up quite suddenly in my mind after re-reading and pondering a bit about Mage's history, the old ages, consensus and reality zones.<br /> Now, bear with me here:<br /> <br /> We all know that, once upon a time, mystical Magick was more 'accepted' than newfangled Hypertech. The Order Of Reason's devices and inventions once had the disadvantage over the Tradition's (and Pre-Tradition's) mystical workings. Heck, even the Order Of Reason did not *quite* start out with *just* technological elements. Their earlier works included things like sacred geometry, mystical alchemy and such items.<br /> Now, over time the Order Of reason changed the global view on things. They managed to first convince society's leaders to accept their ways, then slowly worked their idea of 'science' down to the masses. Bit by bit, certain applications of Hypertech become easier to do, while the mystics found that their more arcane Magicks were on the decline - harder to pull off. The Scourge was on the rise.<br /> Fast forward to modern day, where over the centuries, all sorts of what was once considered vulgar Hypertech has become normal technology - things that every mortal can use. Cars, computers, phones, mobile devices, complex factory machinery, electic household appliances, and-what-not.<br /> <br /> We know all that. But what if, in ancient ages past, long before the Order Of Reason came to be, mystical Magick had an equivalent?<br /> What if something existed that is to mystical Magick, what technology is to Hypertech?<br /> And what if it *still does* exist to this day?<br /> <br /> Numina.<br /> <br /> Think about it. Numina are 'magic' that every mortal can use and learn. They follow rules and their use can be taught - either by a teacher, or through study of books. Let's call them 'manuals'.<br /> Almost every splat can technically use them. They, too, at times require an energy source - not technology's electricity, but Numina's mana.<br /> And just like how technology can mysteriously start to malfunction in the depths of the wild, so can Numina malfunction if a witnesses in modern society is near.<br /> <br /> I consider it kind of a fascinating idea that Numina are very much the remains of what ancient, pre-Tradition Mages scattered over the world once taught some mortals in their tribal villages to make life easier for them - much like the Union did to the first villages and cities in the Renaissance. Numina would be what happens if ritualistic, formalized ways of pulling off a mystic Magickal effect get accepted by the local consensus - so much that, at that point, normal mortals can do it by going through the same steps.<br /> And just like Hypertech stops violating reality as it becomes technology, so does a mystic Magickal effect once it becomes a Numina.<br /> <br /> <br /> I dunno, it's just something that popped up in my head, and it makes way too much sense not to play around with that idea <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 11-16-2024, 11:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-16T09:41:34-08:00","id":1546001,"title":"","content":"What exactly is Numina?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-16T12:39:32-08:00","id":1546006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546000-a-theory-hypertech-and-technology-mystical-magick-and?p=1546001#post1546001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What exactly is Numina?</div> </div> </div> </div>Minor &quot;magics.&quot; Psionics, Sorcery, hedge magic, and similar weak, but not useless magics. If Magick and Hypertech are jets, Numia are bicycles. A sly competent user of Numina can take down a Mage, but the magical power advantage is with the Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-16T14:19:04-08:00","id":1546008,"title":"","content":"Also called 'Linear Magic' because it lacks the more open-ended mix &amp; match possibilities of True Magick. A key point is that Numina <i>usually</i> don't cause Paradox, which if I understood <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6606_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6606\" data-vbnamecard=\"6606\">Ambrosia</a> correctly may hint at that they were once fully part of the Consensus.<br /> <br /> I think some of that is very obvious. The further you go back, the more isolated societies become and I believe Consensus used to be a more localized phenomenon. Culture and religion made up a large part of what certain truths of reality were.<br /> Of course you get a Shaman to exorcise a Disease Spirit. You bury you relatives in your house's foundation, so they still can be around family as ghosts. Many Numina deal with entities that are established lore in the WOD, and those are probably the easiest to trace back to being part of the accepted reality. I mean, they used to be accepted reality in Reality, so no reason they wouldn't have been.<br /> <br /> But, a quote from M20 Sorcerer:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sorcerers do not suffer from Paradox, as they work within the confines of fundamental reality, rather than bending reality to their will. </div> </div> </div>Within the WOD, that means anything a Sorcerer does (or more generally a mortal who uses a Numen) is a-ok with reality. And that includes throwing fireballs, teleportation, and calling lightning from the sky.<br /> I don't think this can be easily equated with Hypertech becoming normal technology, since all these effects (if not masked by an accepted paradigm) would be considered vulgar under the current Consensus. While I agree Numina used to be more integrated in general societal acceptance, the books make a point that they simply <i>are </i>part of the WOD reality, like a vampire's Disciplines or.. vampires.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-16T15:01:48-08:00","id":1546009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546000-a-theory-hypertech-and-technology-mystical-magick-and?p=1546008#post1546008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think this can be easily equated with Hypertech becoming normal technology, since all these effects (if not masked by an accepted paradigm) would be considered vulgar under the current Consensus. While I agree Numina used to be more integrated in general societal acceptance, the books make a point that they simply <i>are </i>part of the WOD reality,<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I forgot which book mentions technology failing in some remote amazon basin technically being kind of a sort of reality-rejection, but the same *can* be said for Numina: In Sorceror, effects are more likely to fail if there are disbelieving witnesses. Just like technology gets harder to use in more mystical-inclined realty zones. In neither case does the user get hit by paradox, but in both cases, things soft-fail.<br /> Perhaps exactly *because* somewhere else in the world in terms of general reality zones, they *are* accepted.<br /> <br /> A vampire's Disciplines, a Werewolf's gifts, etc. on the other hand, are *completely* decoupled from any reality zone or beliefs. Numina, just like technology, don't have that luxury.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 11-16-2024, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-17T04:40:41-08:00","id":1546021,"title":"","content":"That's a good point. In my view, it illustrates that consensual reality and fundamental reality can be at odds sometimes, meaning I see consensual reality (&quot;People can't throw fireballs&quot;) like a 'force' opposing fundamental reality (&quot;They totally can!&quot;).<br /> <br /> So the question here is whether the tree still makes a sound if it falls and no one is around to hear it. A primal place rejects technology regardless of witnesses, but the same mechanism - as far as I know - is not true for a Numen effect.<br /> <br /> I guess the point I'm trying to make is that Magick by definition is a force opposed to reality, and that includes normalized Hypertech - the normalization here being that a piece of consensual reality was pushed very close to or even partially overlapping with fundamental reality, but never congruent. As I understand it, Numina come from the fundamental side of reality and may conflict with the consensual part of it - kind of the inverse scenario.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-18T14:05:48-08:00","id":1546087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546000-a-theory-hypertech-and-technology-mystical-magick-and?p=1546009#post1546009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I forgot which book mentions technology failing in some remote amazon basin technically being kind of a sort of reality-rejection, but the same *can* be said for Numina: In Sorceror, effects are more likely to fail if there are disbelieving witnesses. Just like technology gets harder to use in more mystical-inclined realty zones. In neither case does the user get hit by paradox, but in both cases, things soft-fail.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in M20.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M20, pg 615</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deep Wilderness: True wilderness is hard to find these days, but scraps of it still exist between the cracks of the 21st century. And as anyone who\u2019s ever taken a deep-woods hike can attest, things just work differently out there. <b>Advanced technology tends to fail in deep-wilderness areas, but the oldest forms of magick thrive.</b> The further a person gets from civilization, the less predictable Reality becomes. Werewolves and other monsters favor such remote locations because the hand of humanity still holds very little power there.</div> </div> </div> </div>The section on Rural Areas on pg 614 also makes it clear that these reality zones do not just apply to hypertech, but to regular technology.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546000-a-theory-hypertech-and-technology-mystical-magick-and?p=1546021#post1546021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a good point. In my view, it illustrates that consensual reality and fundamental reality can be at odds sometimes, meaning I see consensual reality (&quot;People can't throw fireballs&quot;) like a 'force' opposing fundamental reality (&quot;They totally can!&quot;).<br /> <br /> So the question here is whether the tree still makes a sound if it falls and no one is around to hear it. A primal place rejects technology regardless of witnesses, but the same mechanism - as far as I know - is not true for a Numen effect.<br /> <br /> I guess the point I'm trying to make is that Magick by definition is a force opposed to reality, and that includes normalized Hypertech - the normalization here being that a piece of consensual reality was pushed very close to or even partially overlapping with fundamental reality, but never congruent. As I understand it, Numina come from the fundamental side of reality and may conflict with the consensual part of it - kind of the inverse scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know that I'd firmly separate Consensual Reality and Fundamental reality like that. Mage hasn't given a firm explanation of how this works, so I suppose it could, but its not the only or (in my opinion) the best relationship between the two. I think there is room for Consensus reality to permanently reshape fundamental reality if it pushes long enough or strong enough. But all that depends on what Fundamental Reality is or how it is defined, which tends to vary between readers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}